### Part 1 — AI cruft (8 findings)
1. app/app/menu/page.js:42  vague name `data` → rename to `menuItems`.
2. app/app/page.js:188  empty `catch {}` swallows an image-load error → log with context.
3. app/app/about/page.js:33 inline `style={{ padding: '40px 0' }}` → use `.section` from globals.
4. app/app/page.js:212 commented-out "old hero" block left behind → delete.
5. app/app/contact/page.js:55 phrasing "We are pleased to offer comprehensive café services" — off-brand → suggest F1 voice ("Pull into the pit lane for…").
6. app/app/gallery/page.js:88 useEffect copies `images` prop into state — remove, render prop directly.
...

### Part 2 — Reuse opportunities (3 findings)
1. WhatsApp `<a>` block duplicated 5×: Navbar.js, Footer.js, page.js (×2 — hero CTA + final CTA), contact/page.js.
   → Extract app/app/components/WhatsAppButton.js with props { label, className }.
2. Address block hardcoded 3×: page.js (about preview section), contact/page.js, Footer.js.
   → Move to app/app/lib/site-info.js: `ADDRESS = "Lot 8155 & 8156, Section 64, Jalan Simpang Tiga, Kuching"`.
3. F1-tag markup re-implemented inline in 4 sections; `.f1-tag` already exists in globals.css.
   → Replace inline markup with `<span className="f1-tag">…</span>`.

### Recommended cleanup order
P0: 1, 2 (WhatsApp + address consolidation — these will diverge silently next time the number / address changes).
P1: Part 1 #5 (off-brand copy is visible on first load).
P2: Part 1 #1, #6 (rename + remove useEffect anti-pattern).
```

## Rules

- Don't extract a component used in only two places — three is the threshold.
- Don't replace `<ScrollReveal>` with a custom abstraction.
- Don't rename a variable that is part of an exported component API without updating callers.
- Don't recommend Lodash / Ramda — vanilla `Array.prototype` is enough for this scale of site.
- Don't sanitize the F1 brand voice into "professional café marketing" — it's the project's intentional tone.
- You are read-only — return findings; do not modify code.
